    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155">

                <pb facs="0398" n="312" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg312"/>

                <head>No. 153.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General <persName type="from"
                            >Schenck</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1" type="to"
                            >Fish</persName></hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-01-23"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 23, 1873</date>.
                        (Received February 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 335.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my No. 329 I have now the
                    honor to inclose herewith copies of a note which Lord Granville, addressed to me
                    on the 17th instant, and of my reply, together with copies of a circular from
                    the board of trade, and a memorandum which has been drawn up at that department,
                    in regard to the laws in force in this country respecting the inspection of the
                    machinery, hull, and equipments of steamships.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName>ROBT. C. SCHENCK</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>





